{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.ContentProductRows","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ContentProductRows","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HookProductMonoidBridge"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_mul_descFactF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_mul_descFactF","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ContentProductRows.lean#L94-L111","doc":"**The content side, division-free.**\n\n`∏_{c ∈ μ} f(r − c₁ + c₂) · ∏_{i<r} descFactF f (r−1−i) = ∏_{i<r} descFactF f (r − i + μ_i − 1)`.\n\nThe right-hand product is `∏_i descFactF f β_i` at `r` rows — the *same* object the hook side\nproduces (`SYTBetaGapVandermonde.prodHooksF_mul_pair_prod`).  Dividing the two therefore cancels it,\nleaving the Vandermonde over a `μ`-independent constant: exactly the shape the branching ratio needs.\n\nThe left-hand correction `∏_{i<r} descFactF f (r−1−i)` is `μ`-independent, so it cancels too when the\nratio of two diagrams is taken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_rows_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_rows_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ContentProductRows.lean#L83-L90","doc":"**The q-instance, in `schurPrincipal`'s own `zpow` form.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.schurNumExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.schurNumExponent","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ContentProductRows.lean#L70-L81","doc":"On a cell of a diagram with at most `r` rows, `schurPrincipal`'s integer exponent\n`r + content c` is the natural number `r − c₁ + c₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodContentF_rows","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ContentProductRows.lean#L46-L68","doc":"**The content product, reindexed by rows.**\n\n`∏_{c ∈ μ.cells} f(r − c₁ + c₂) = ∏_{i < r} ∏_{j < rowLen i} f(r − i + j)`.\n\nThe outer range is `r`, so the statement is already in the zero-padded convention: rows past the last\nnonzero one contribute an empty product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowLen_eq_zero_of_colLen_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.rowLen_eq_zero_of_colLen_le","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ContentProductRows.lean#L39-L44","doc":"Rows past `colLen 0` are empty. ","signatureChunk":0}]}